// Baseline for the default headless scenario (issue #868).
//
// Recorded from three release runs of `--sim-seconds 60` against
// assets/worlds/default.toml. Run-to-run spread on one machine was under 3%.
//
// PROVENANCE WARNING: these numbers were recorded on a developer desktop, not
// on the CI runner that compares against them. A GitHub-hosted runner is
// materially slower, so the first CI captures are expected to warn until this
// file is re-recorded from one of them. That is survivable precisely because
// the comparison is warnings-only and gates nothing — re-record from a CI
// capture artifact, in its own reviewable commit, before anyone considers
// promoting Verdict::Fail to a merge gate.
//
// Tolerances are wider than vellum-perf's defaults (0.25 / 1.0) for the same
// reason: a tolerance that cries wolf gets ignored rather than obeyed, and
// this one is knowingly calibrated against the wrong machine.
//
// sim.tick is held at p95 rather than max on purpose. The first tick of a run
// loads assets and costs 35-46ms; that is startup, not steady-state simulation,
// and a max-based expectation would measure the loader.
(
    scenario: "headless-default",
    expectations: {
        "sim.tick": (
            unit: millis,
            statistic: p95,
            expected: 0.78,
            tolerance: (warn: 0.5, fail: 2.0),
        ),
        "sim.run": (
            unit: seconds,
            statistic: mean,
            expected: 2.40,
            tolerance: (warn: 0.5, fail: 2.0),
        ),
    },
)
